  "notes": [
    "All capacity values are expressed in decimal Exabytes (1 EB = 10^18 bytes = 10^9 GB) of NATIVE (uncompressed) storage shipped in that calendar year.",
    "Consistency identity: price (USD/GB) = revenue (USD_B) / capacity (EB). Across all 47 years (1980–2026) for both HDD and Tape, |price - revenue/capacity| / price is within 2%.",
    "HDD unit shipments peaked in 2010 (~651–652M units, 330 EB, $33.0B), whereas HDD industry revenue peaked in 2012 ($37.5B, 380 EB) due to supply shortages and elevated ASPs following the late-2011 Thailand floods.",
    "After a severe cyclical downturn in 2023 (127M units, 897 EB, $13.4B), AI data center nearline demand drove a sharp rebound in 2024 (1,340 EB, $19.8B), 2025 (1,620 EB, $23.3B), and 2026E (~2,060 EB, ~$34.9B).",
    "Tape series follow the Fontana & Decad (IBM Systems, MSST 2018 / Library of Congress 2019) definition: worldwide magnetic tape media (cartridge) revenue (USD_B), native (uncompressed) tape media capacity shipped (EB), and native cartridge cost per GB (USD/GB). LTO Program compressed capacity figures for 2018–2026 are converted to native capacity using the standard 2.5:1 compression factor (e.g., 2024 record 176.5 EB compressed = 70.6 EB native; 2025 160.3 EB compressed = 64.1 EB native). Combined tape ecosystem revenue (including tape drives and automated libraries, e.g., $1.56B in 2010 per SCCG) is documented in hdd_tape.md."
